      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge beat Callington by 6 wickets to remain top of County Division 1. Callington made a swift start in excellent batting conditions at Egloshayle Park, openers Aidan Libby (38) and Alex Robinson (30) adding 68-0 in 13.2 overs before a rain delay which reduced the match to 40 overs per side. Alek Gill (3-22) struck crucial blows upon the resumption to help slow the rate, but Andrew Jones (35), Joe White (42) and Adam Welcome (32*) helped Callington post 221-7. Half centuries from Matt Jolliffe (55) and James Maycock (67) kept the Swans up with the rate as they added a third century opening partnership (125) of the season. Callington sensed a chance after removing both, but Wadebridge eased home with 17 deliveries to spare on the back of fluent runs from Charlie McLachlan (32), Barny Jackson (30) and Cal Morse (22*).",
